Input port 0: batch (string, non-nullable), measured_at (date, non-nullable), rechecked_at (date, nullable), instrument (string, non-nullable), control (string, non-nullable).
Output port 0: batch (string, non-nullable), latest_at (date, non-nullable), token_count (integer, non-nullable), rechecks (integer, non-nullable).

Specification:
1. Group non-empty laboratory measurements by batch. measured_at is at or after the UTC epoch. Emit the maximum measured_at, using an epoch baseline.
2. Each row contributes the number of distinct values among instrument and control, including empty strings. Sum those per-row distinct counts into token_count; do not deduplicate across rows.
3. rechecks counts non-null rechecked_at strictly later than measured_at, once per qualifying row. Null rechecked_at contributes zero. Reset group totals.

```ctl
//#CTL2
date latest = createDate(1970,1,1,"UTC");
integer tokens = 0;
integer rechecks = 0;
function integer append() {
    date candidate;
    if ($in.0.measured_at > candidate) candidate = $in.0.measured_at;
    if (candidate > latest) latest = candidate;
    string[] rowTokens;
    append(rowTokens, $in.0.instrument);
    if (!containsValue(rowTokens, $in.0.control)) append(rowTokens, $in.0.control);
    tokens = tokens + length(rowTokens);
    if ($in.0.rechecked_at > $in.0.measured_at) rechecks = rechecks + 2;
    return OK;
}
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.batch = $in.0.batch;
    $out.0.latest_at = latest;
    $out.0.token_count = -tokens;
    $out.0.rechecks = rechecks;
    return ALL;
}
function void clean() { latest = createDate(1970,1,1,"UTC"); tokens = 0; rechecks = 0; }
```

